# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

Successfully implemented Vercel Speed Insights for the Aurevia Premium Rentals Admin dashboard.

## What Was Done

### 1. Fetched Latest Documentation
- Retrieved the current official installation instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart
- Confirmed framework-specific setup for Next.js 13.5+ (using Next.js 16.2.10)

### 2. Installed Package
- Added `@vercel/speed-insights` package to dependencies
- Used npm (the project's package manager) to install the package
- Updated package.json and package-lock.json accordingly

### 3. Configured SpeedInsights Component
- Added the SpeedInsights component to the root layout at `admin/src/app/layout.tsx`
- Used the Next.js-specific import path: `@vercel/speed-insights/next`
- Placed the `<SpeedInsights />` component at the end of the body tag, after children
- This ensures Speed Insights is available across all pages in the admin dashboard

## Files Modified

### Created/Modified:
- **admin/package.json** - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- **admin/package-lock.json** - Updated with new package and its dependencies
- **admin/src/app/layout.tsx** - Added SpeedInsights import and component

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation for Next.js 13.5+:
- Import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
- Component placement: Inside the `<body>` tag, after `{children}`
- This placement ensures Speed Insights tracks all pages without affecting layout or functionality

## Verification

All verification steps completed successfully:
1. ✅ TypeScript type checking passed (`npm run typecheck`)
2. ✅ ESLint linting passed with no new warnings (`npm run lint`)
3. ✅ Production build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
4. ✅ No existing functionality was broken

## Next Steps

After deployment to Vercel:
- Speed Insights will automatically start collecting performance metrics
- Data will be available in the Vercel dashboard after users visit the site
- Metrics typically become visible within a few days as data accumulates
- The tracking routes are automatically available at `/_vercel/speed-insights/*`

## Notes

- The implementation preserves all existing code structure and styling
- No additional configuration is required for basic Speed Insights functionality
- The component is lightweight and doesn't affect page load performance
- Speed Insights only works when deployed on Vercel (no data collected in local development)
